  "answer": "Runny nose and a mild cough with no fever, two days in, is most often a common cold. Colds usually last about a week and can run up to 2 weeks. Extra fluids and rest help, and if they're drinking and playing, watching at home is reasonable.",
  "triage": "Call 811 for ear pain, a fever, much more sleepiness or fussiness, or if it lasts past 10-14 days. Go to the ER or call 911 now for fast or hard breathing, ribs pulling in, blue lips, or if they're hard to wake.",
  "sources": ["Canadian Paediatric Society (Caring for Kids)", "Seattle Children's", "Children's Healthcare of Atlanta"]
}
